WEBVTT

NOTE week06-clip1-masked-reconstruction
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.376 line:2 align:center
We start with a single lead ECG
recording, ten seconds long.

2
00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:10.483 line:2 align:center
Nobody has labeled it with a diagnosis,
so all we have is the raw signal.

3
00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:15.771 line:2 align:center
We cut the signal into one second
patches. Just like words in a sentence,

4
00:00:15.771 --> 00:00:20.750 line:2 align:center
each patch becomes one token
for a transformer encoder.

5
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.299 line:2 align:center
Then we hide most of
the patches at random.

6
00:00:24.299 --> 00:00:29.017 line:2 align:center
Here, six of the ten
patches are masked out.

7
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:32.594 line:2 align:center
The encoder sees only
the four visible patches,

8
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:36.750 line:2 align:center
and turns each of them
into an embedding vector.

9
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.444 line:2 align:center
A small decoder takes these embeddings,

10
00:00:39.444 --> 00:00:43.361 line:2 align:center
plus a placeholder mask
token for every hidden patch,

11
00:00:43.361 --> 00:00:46.350 line:2 align:center
and predicts the missing waveform.

12
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:51.677 line:2 align:center
The loss is the mean squared error between
the prediction and the true signal,

13
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:56.017 line:2 align:center
computed only on the
patches that were hidden.

14
00:00:56.217 --> 00:01:02.065 line:2 align:center
Over many training steps, the predictions
improve. To fill the gaps well,

15
00:01:02.065 --> 00:01:07.737 line:2 align:center
the encoder has to learn the structure of
a heartbeat: the P wave, the QRS complex,

16
00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:10.617 line:2 align:center
and the T wave.

17
00:01:10.817 --> 00:01:15.047 line:2 align:center
After pretraining, the decoder
has done its job and is discarded.

18
00:01:15.047 --> 00:01:22.017 line:2 align:center
We keep the encoder, which now produces
useful representations of ECG signals.

19
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:24.153 line:2 align:center
The same recipe works for pathology.

20
00:01:24.153 --> 00:01:30.847 line:2 align:center
A masked autoencoder hides most
patches of an H&E tile, here 12 of 16,

21
00:01:30.847 --> 00:01:34.647 line:2 align:center
and learns to reconstruct
the missing pixels.
